# You normally do NOT need to create a .env file any more.
#
# The two environments are committed and selected automatically by NODE_ENV:
#
#   .env.development   `expo start` + debug builds   -> local API
#   .env.production    `assembleRelease`, `expo export`, `eoas publish`
#                                                    -> the deployed API
#
# Copy this file only when you need to override the local URL for your own
# machine — most often because you are running on a PHYSICAL device, which
# cannot reach the emulator's 10.0.2.2 alias and needs your LAN IP:
#
#   cp apps/mobile/.env.example apps/mobile/.env.development.local
#
# `.env.development.local` is gitignored and beats `.env.development`, but only
# for development — it can never leak into a release APK. Do not use a plain
# `.env.local` for this: that one overrides production builds too.
#
# Find your LAN IP with `ipconfig` (Windows) and confirm the phone is on the
# same network with no VPN splitting the two.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL="http://192.168.1.10:3000"
